    <item>
      <title></title>
      <link>https://people.csail.mit.edu/weifang/authors/admin/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 12 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://people.csail.mit.edu/weifang/authors/admin/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;I am a final year PhD candidate in the Spoken Language Systems Group at MIT CSAIL, advised by &lt;a href=&#34;http://people.csail.mit.edu/jrg/&#34;&gt;Dr. James Glass&lt;/a&gt;. I will soon be joining &lt;a href=&#34;https://subconscious.dev&#34;&gt;Subconscious&lt;/a&gt; as an AI Scientist to build efficient, long-context LLM agents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My research focuses on augmented and agentic LLMs, with an emphasis on improving LLM agents&#39; retrieval and tool-use capabilities and efficiency. I have also worked on knowledge-grounded AI, aiming to ground models in factual and structured knowledge, and I am broadly interested in generative AI and machine learning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I hold a Master&amp;rsquo;s degree from MIT, where I worked on automatic fact verification and speech synthesis under Dr. Glass. I received my Bachelor&amp;rsquo;s degree from National Taiwan University (NTU), working on speech and language understanding with &lt;a href=&#34;http://speech.ee.ntu.edu.tw/~tlkagk/&#34;&gt;Prof. Hung-Yi Lee&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&#34;http://speech.ee.ntu.edu.tw/previous_version/lslNew.htm&#34;&gt;Prof. Lin-Shan Lee&lt;/a&gt;, and computer vision with &lt;a href=&#34;http://vllab.ee.ntu.edu.tw/members.html&#34;&gt;Prof. Yu-Chiang Frank Wang&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;ve conducted research internships at the MIT-IBM Watson AI Lab in Cambridge, MA, and twice with the NLP team at Apple in Cupertino, CA.&lt;/p&gt;
